                <pb facs="1147" n="1133" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1133"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1470: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-27T19:00:00-04:00">June 27, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>367. The Department assumes that the “good offices” referred to in your telegram
                    no. 402, June 25, 12 noon, relate exclusively to the transmission of messages
                    between the contending factions and do not involve the preparation and
                    submission of formulas of settlement, et cetera.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Mexico and other missions in Central America.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
